  "rules": [
    "Blueprint approval authorizes target construction only, not target execution or an external effect. Record distinct scopes from the same actual user reply only when that reply explicitly covers them; do not re-ask valid authorization.",
    "Blueprint user must/emphasis changes require exact old/new hash and changed-ID amendment authority. Historical originals remain in blueprint_history. Product must changes similarly pin prior/new definition hash and scope requirement:ID.",
    "Canonical authority binding supports only foundry-authority/1. Denied/revoked/changed source is blocked. Unsupported authority formats are rejected; prepare a current record from actual authority, without adapters or reinterpretation. Hashes do not authenticate a human.",
    "Task readiness enforces current execution scope, current musts, phase prerequisites, dependencies, knowledge, sources, suite and pauses. Pending requirements may be fulfilled by the task; every declared requirement closes individually before completion.",
    "Evidence binds exact current artifacts/proof/test definitions. Independent tests reject self-observation. A file/hash/declared observer is not proof of actual professional, device, media or provider quality.",
    "Bundle-check uses exact approved skill set, expected unpacked artifact paths and every current blueprint test pass. The final ZIP/self-checksum must not be defined as a required artifact inside itself.",
    "Register external grants for exactly one action_id/idempotency_key. Dispatch writes pending before host tool use and executes nothing. Unknown outcomes require actual read-only reconciliation proof, not retry.",
    "Pause now or after exact artifact/task/phase blocks new work gates; safe receipt/evidence/checkpoint recording remains possible. Resume never replays completed work or effects.",
    "Intake accepts separate source directories/ZIPs, rejects links/traversal/case collisions/special files, max10000 files and256MiB decompressed per intake. Use separately verified bounded chunks or pinned external storage for larger inputs.",
    "Runtime Python3.9+ uses POSIX locking on Linux/macOS; actual host/tool/device/account support must be verified. No command invokes an LLM, background service, imported executable or external action.",
    "Every catalog topic has source-linked applicability/rationale/current status/owner/due coverage; current construction unknowns block approval. Future product decisions are resolved in separate project decision records at their due phase, without reapproving unchanged agent capabilities.",
    "Independent tasks may fulfill separate pending musts in parallel. Explicit required inputs/blocks_work/blocks_task_ids and due material decisions gate dependent starts; every current phase must/emphasis and due test closes at phase-check.",
    "A previously bound canonical authority cannot be dropped or redirected in a sidecar update. Update/reconcile its current canonical source or perform an explicit separately reviewed migration; do not reinterpret a denial.",
    "Capability availability alone does not authorize an effect: effect_types and exact capability scope must cover the proposed grant. Previous typed record revisions are retained in record_history.",
    "Current source protocol and command contract are described by foundry.py --help and the runtime interface shipped with the delivery. Use distinct factory/project session roots; do not reinitialize an existing ledger."
  ]
}
